    {
      "id": "switch-jump-table",
      "rule": "MSC 7 compiles a dense `switch` into `cmp ax,N; ja default; shl ax,1; xchg bx,ax; jmp word ptr cs:[bx+T]` with the N+1 case offsets stored as `dw` rows right after the jump (the packet shows them as `dw offset X`; the cases are `sub`-normalised so `sub ax,5; cmp ax,8` means cases 5..13 with holes pointing at `default`). Write a plain `switch` on the value with exactly those case labels; holes are absent cases, shared targets are fall-through or identical labels, `default:` only when the ja target does real work. Case body order follows the source order; `break` tails become `jmp` to the common exit and each body except the last is followed by an alignment `nop`. Sparse switches compile to compare chains instead; do not force a table.",
